{
 "_about": "What each tutor and recursion entry of the 15 decks with a combo check may supply, as the owner-accepted step-1 tag checklist (2026-11-24, 113 lines; plan 'combo checks, step 1') states it in its 'Step 1' column, written by hand from that column, not from the exporter; the entries the combo-line corrections (owner decision 27, 2026-11-25) change were written by hand from each entry's tags and the approved line blocks, under the same routes ('combo-line corrections' below). Per deck, per entry: 'combo' maps each deck-file piece (winConditions kind combo) the entry can supply to its routes ('hand': the card goes to the hand or is cast from the graveyard, and the piece is paid; 'battlefield': put onto the battlefield, not paid; 'bargain': Beseech the Mirror bargained, cast free); 'assembly' maps each KEY_COMBOS line the entry can fill a slot of to the members it can fetch, by name (for 'any member', every member of the line the deck holds, as the deck headers of the owner's checklist name them; for witherbloom-the-balancer and zada-hedron-grinder, whose headers there do not list each line's members, as the full checklist the owner's copy summarises names them). An empty object: the entry supplies nothing in step 1. The 9 lands and the recursion entries of creeping-corruption and witherbloom-the-balancer are not checklist lines; they supply nothing. Combo-line corrections: anvil-chorus and armory-protocol keep no combo line (W1, W2), so their recursion entries (Master Skald; Emry, Lurker of the Loch) are no longer listed, 111 lines in all; a castFromHand piece (Dualcaster Mage) has no battlefield route; a list in a line's pieces, or a slot added without cast priority, supplies each of its cards like any piece or member. Deck removal (2026-11-27): the blocks of armory-protocol (5 lines), gandalf-party-guest (7), grave-dividends (29) and shield-doctrine (7) were removed with their decks; 11 decks and 63 lines remain, and no other block changed.",
